Find KE of product particles in,
Pi(+) = mu(+) + nu
here Pi(+) is stationary.
Rest mass of Pi(+) & mu(+) is 139.6 MeV & 105.7 MeV respectively.

Choices:
A. 7.2 MeV, 32.8 MeV
B. 4.12 MeV, 29.8 MeV
C. 2.84 MeV, 26.8 MeV
D. 3.52 MeV, 20.8 MeV

Solve the question. At the end, write exactly one final line in this format and do not write anything after it:
Answer: <letter>
QUESTION_PROMPT_END
MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=847
We have the decay:
π⁺ → μ⁺ + ν_μ  
with π⁺ at rest.

Given:
m_π = 139.6 MeV/c²  
m_μ = 105.7 MeV/c²  
m_ν ≈ 0

Energy conservation:
m_π c² = E_μ + E_ν  
Momentum conservation (magnitudes equal):
p_μ = p_ν

For the neutrino: E_ν = p_ν c  
For the muon: E_μ = √(p_μ² c² + m_μ² c⁴)

Let p = p_μ c = p_ν c (in energy units). Then:

E_μ = √(p² + m_μ²)  
E_ν = p

Energy conservation:
√(p² + m_μ²) + p = m_π

Solve:
√(p² + m_μ²) = m_π - p  
Square:
p² + m_μ² = m_π² - 2 m_π p + p²  
⇒ m_μ² = m_π² - 2 m_π p  
⇒ 2 m_π p = m_π² - m_μ²  
⇒ p = (m_π² - m_μ²) / (2 m_π)

Compute numerically:
m_π² = (139.6)² = 19488.16  
m_μ² = (105.7)² = 11172.49  
Difference = 19488.16 - 11172.49 = 8315.67  
Divide by 2 m_π = 279.2 → p = 8315.67 / 279.2 ≈ 29.78 MeV

Thus:
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

